cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If this tool informs a paper, a thesis, a lecture or a studio brief, please cite it as software."
type: software
title: "Daylight Lab: A browser-based daylight simulation tool"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-16
abstract: >-
  A daylighting analysis tool for architecture students that runs entirely in
  the browser, shipped as a single self-contained HTML file. A parametric room
  with real wall, roof and floor thickness; windows, skylights and doors that
  can be added, sized and moved; horizontal and vertical shading devices; a 3D
  sun path with shadows and visible solar rays; and a workplane grid reporting
  illuminance, daylight factor and useful daylight illuminance, plus daylight
  autonomy, spatial daylight autonomy, annual sunlight exposure and direct sun
  hours. Two independent engines are provided — a Monte-Carlo raytracer using
  daylight coefficients over Tregenza/Reinhart sky patches, and a BRE
  split-flux implementation following BS 8206-2 — and their agreement is
  measured and published.
